# The flip of cyc_pd with an amplitude dependent frequency, z' = (beta + i (Om + kap |w|^2)) z
# - |z|^2 z with kap = 0.8. In the frame q = w exp(-i arg(z) / 2) the equations for q and |z|
# do not depend on the angle, and q' = lam q + eps r conj(q) - gam |q|^2 q - i kap |q|^2 q / 2.
# The flip is still at beta = 1/4. The cubic term of the center manifold gets no
# contribution from the change of the return time, which is of fifth order, so
# c = -gam / T = -1/pi as for cyc_pd. The coefficient alpha1 of the period is nonzero, so
# this tests the terms of the periodic normalization that carry it. Own test model.
par beta=0.2
Om=2
r2=x2^2+y2^2
fr=Om+0.8*r2
x1'=beta*x1-fr*y1-(x1^2+y1^2)*x1
y1'=beta*y1+fr*x1-(x1^2+y1^2)*y1
x2'=-0.5*x2-0.5*Om*y2+(x1*x2+y1*y2)-r2*x2
y2'=-0.5*y2+0.5*Om*x2+(y1*x2-x1*y2)-r2*y2
init x1=0.45,y1=0,x2=0,y2=0
done
